\citation{guo2026tgmp}
\citation{peng2021amp}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of SG-AMP. Three lightweight modifications are made on top of vanilla AMP: (1) the style reward is gated by the CoP-based stability margin $g(m_t)$; (2) the discriminator is conditioned on the gait phase $(\cos \phi _t,\sin \phi _t)$; and (3) the style weight $\lambda _t=\lambda _{\max }\cdot \bar  g_t$ follows an EMA of the gate. All signals are available from the physics backend (Isaac Sim PhysX for training, MuJoCo for sim2sim).}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{3}{}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces CoP-gated style reward (contribution 1). The CoP is computed from contact forces, and the minimum signed distance $m_t$ to the support-polygon edges defines a dynamic stability margin. The smooth gate $g(m_t)=\sigma ((m_t-m_0)/\kappa )$ scales the AMP style reward so style supervision is active only when the robot is dynamically stable.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cop}{{2}{3}{}{figure.2}{}}
